                        "mmol_l": 41.9013,
                        "optional": 0
                    },
                    {
                        "recipe_order": 9,
                        "compound": "Colloidal chitin",
                        "compound_id": 1506,
                        "amount": 5,
                        "unit": "g",
                        "g_l": 5,
                        "optional": 0
                    },
                    {
                        "recipe_order": 10,
                        "compound": "Distilled water",
                        "compound_id": 4,
                        "amount": 890,
                        "unit": "ml",
                        "optional": 0
                    }
                ],
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "step": "<b>Reducing agents</b>: \r\nFlush each solution under N2 for 30 minutes, stopper and autoclave.\r\nL-Cysteine-HCL x H2O solution (10%): add 12.5 \u00b5l per 10 ml medium\r\nNa2S x 9 H2O solution (3%): add 40 \u00b5l per 10 ml medium."
                    },
                    {
                        "step": "<b>Colloidal chitin preparation</b>: \r\nCut 5 gram commercial crab (shrimp) shell flakes into small pieces, and dissolve in 100\r\nml of 12M HCL while stirring in a fume hood at room temperature. Add chitin-HCL\r\nmixture slowly into pre-cooled water to obtain the colloidal chitin, centrifuge and wash in\r\npre-cooled water till the colloidal chitin reaches a pH of 6 to 6.5. Mix 0.5% with MS\r\nmedium as the sole carbon source. As an alternative commercial available chitin powder\r\ncan be used."
                    },
                    {
                        "step": "<b>Prepare MS medium with chitin</b>: \r\nDissolve the ingredients of MS medium (except NaHCO3 and vitamins), boil medium\r\nunder CO2 until the resazurin indicator changes from pink to colourless. Cool down under\r\nCO2, add NaHCO3 and adjust pH to 7.0. Switch to N2 to prevent further lowering of the\r\npH. Fill up into Hungate tubes under N2 and autoclave. Before use add vitamins\r\n(sterilized by filtration) and reducing agents."
                    }
                ],
                "equipment": {
                    "4676": "Filter",
                    "4677": "Hungate tubes",
                    "4678": "Autoclave",
                    "4679": "Gassing station"
                }
            },
